  "title": "The Complete Guide to Multi-Lender Marketplace Platforms",
  "summary": "A multi-lender marketplace is a digital platform that connects borrowers to multiple financial institutions through a single application, enabling side-by-side comparison of financing offers without submitting separate applications to each lender. These platforms use automated routing and waterfall logic to match borrowers with lenders whose criteria fit their profile, increasing approval odds while protecting credit scores through soft-pull prequalification.",
